# tools/ales_session_witness.rish — the session file (ALES39).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES39.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-155054_fill-ales39-lotus-session.md
# Stands on: lotus/seal.rye (ALES38) — begin/finish/open reused whole as the whole-project integrity frame; lotus/rack_sheet.rye
# (ALES33) and lotus/cue_sheet.rye (ALES22) — render/parse reused whole as the two sections; lotus/rack.rye (ALES30) and
# lotus/markers.rye (ALES20) — the two structures a project bundles.
#
# lotus/session.rye bundles a keeper's whole project — the rack (held audio spans) AND the cue sheet (the arrangement map) over one
# master — into a single sealed document, so the two halves can never drift apart into two files from different takes. The crux: a
# session document round-trips the whole project AND the whole document verifies before either half is trusted — save renders a byte-
# length manifest then the two records verbatim and seals the whole, and load runs seal.open over the ENTIRE body (refusing
# DigestMismatch before a single slot or marker is parsed) then splits by the manifest so parse_rack and parse_sheet each see EXACTLY
# their own bytes. The body is length-delimited, never delimiter-scanned, because a slot or marker name may hold any character. The
# selftest proves: a two-slot rack and a four-marker cue sheet over one master round-trip whole; a flipped byte in either the rack half
# or the cue half and a truncated tail each refuse DigestMismatch with both outputs empty; a malformed seal or manifest refuses
# BadRecord; a save into a too-small buffer refuses Overflow. The seal proves a project arrived whole, not who wrote it — no signature,
# no keys, no network, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_session_witness.rish

say "ales-session: Language EN — ALES39 bundles a keeper's whole project into one sealed document: the rack (the held audio) and the cue sheet (the arrangement map) over one master, saved and loaded together so a map can never drift from the audio it names, the whole verified before either half is trusted the way the ALES0 audio wire already keeps a live frame."
say "ales-session: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a session document round-trips the whole project AND the whole document verifies before either half is trusted — save seals a manifest plus the two records, and load runs seal.open over the entire body before splitting it, so no tampered project reaches either parser."
say "ales-session: Lens TAME — the body is length-delimited, never delimiter-scanned (a name may hold any character), and the manifest carries its own check (the payload must measure exactly rack_len + cue_len); seal.begin/finish/open and rack_sheet/cue_sheet render/parse are reused whole; a tampered body refuses DigestMismatch, a malformed seal or manifest refuses BadRecord, a too-small buffer refuses Overflow, each before a slot or marker is trusted; the seal proves a project arrived whole, not who wrote it — no signature, no key; siloed to lotus/, no network, no funds, no device, no meter, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/session"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/session.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-session: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/session.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-session: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-session: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-session' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-session: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-session line"

say "ales-session: GREEN — a keeper's whole project saves and loads as one sealed document: save seals a length manifest plus the rack record and the cue record, and load verifies the whole body before splitting it so each parser sees exactly its own bytes; a two-slot rack and a four-marker cue sheet round-trip whole, a flipped byte in either half or a truncated tail refuses DigestMismatch with both outputs empty, a malformed seal or manifest refuses BadRecord, a too-small buffer refuses Overflow. The purely-local persistence arc is whole — file, edit, save, seal, load, merge, rename, and now one document for the whole project. The SIGNED carry (who wrote a session, via a Kumara key) and the ALES0-wire carry stay module seams for Keaton's word."
